s. Expert raters are split, with several calling the race a Tossup and others Lean D or Likely D, averaging out to a tilt toward Democrats. Prediction markets give Moskowitz roughly a two-in-three chance. No reliable general-election polling exists, so the forecast leans on fundamentals and ratings, leaving meaningful uncertainty in a race expected to hinge on cost-of-living politics and views of the president.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7798, "margin": 4.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7278, "margin": 3.5}]}